; the search and the kernel agree (doc/kurt-soundness.md §10.4): a `sub` of a rule's conclusion
; is checked again with the values of the whole match. "forall-cond-elim" matches its conclusion
; `sub $$v $a %P` first, when `$$v` has no sort yet; its premise `∀ (sub $$x $$v %C) %P` then
; matches `∀ X ∈ Pow(A)`, over the sets. The search put the unsorted `c` in for `X` and the kernel
; rejected the step -- a `KernelError`, which `expect` can't catch (found 2026-10-19 with a variant
; of exercise 03-sets (g)). Now the search refuses it (`sub_sorts_hold`)
load set
set X
const A, B
use ∀ X ∈ Pow(A) (X ∈ Pow(B))
const c
use c ∈ Pow(A)
expect "ProofError"
    c ∈ Pow(B)                  ; `c` has no sort: the fact is about the sets
sandbox
    set d
    use d ∈ Pow(A)
    d ∈ Pow(B)                  ; a set: by "forall-cond-elim"
